WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:08.250
There are six questions you must ask yourself
in order for you to position yourself to dominate

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.250
an industry.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.870
And by the way, today's message is not specific
to any industry.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.510
It can be used for every single industry out
there.

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:15.830
So let's get right into it.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:20.599
The first thing you got to do, wherever you're
currently at with your business, what market

00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:22.330
do you own in your industry?

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.680
So look at the thing and say, "Well, I think
we own this right now.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.999
I think I own this right now.

00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:29.449
I think I own this part of the market right
now.

00:00:29.449 --> 00:00:34.050
Maybe I own this demographic or this age or
this income or this country, or this state

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.340
or whatever it is.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.340
What is it?

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.340
Do you own anything?

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.340
If not, then none.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.340
But whatever you do, write that down.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.399
The next one.

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:41.550
What do you want to own?

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.769
Do you even know what you want to own?

00:00:43.769 --> 00:00:46.520
Is it something where you're clear about what
you want to own?

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.130
Is there an age that you want to own?

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:53.579
Is there a demographic, a culture, an income
earner, a certain city, a certain state, a

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:55.199
certain country?

00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:56.739
What market do you want to own?

00:00:56.739 --> 00:00:58.100
Do you know what market that is?

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.610
That's the second question you've got to answer.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.949
#3: Who must you outgun?

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:04.300
Who must you outgun?

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.140
Who must you outdo?

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.450
Who is leading this market that you want to
own that you must outgun?

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.450
Who are those people?

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.450
Make a list of them.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.450
A, B, C.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.229
This company here, that company here and this
company here.

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:20.119
By the way, this could be you watching this
and you're the CEO of Sprint.

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:23.250
This could be you watching this and you're
a billionaire at of Ohio, okay?

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.920
Several people that watch the Valuetainment
channel.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:32.090
This can be you saying, I want to beat Sprint
or I want to beat Verizon or AT&amp;T or T-Mobile

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:39.939
or it could be you're a liquor store in Little
Rock, Arkansas and you want to own that market

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:44.200
in Little Rock, for you to be the dominant
liquor store in Little Rock, Arkansas, but

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.200
you're not yet.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:52.450
Who must you outgun, and which market do you
want to own - beer, alcohol, vodka, whiskey,

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:55.109
wine, - what is it that you want to own?

00:01:55.109 --> 00:02:01.149
#4: Enough Money - how much money do you need
to outgun, in order for you to get the market

00:02:01.149 --> 00:02:02.149
that you want to own.

00:02:02.149 --> 00:02:03.149
Because it takes money.

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:08.030
It takes money for marketing, for staff, for
executives, for advertising, for technology,

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.980
for speed, for website, for pay per click.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.990
It doesn't matter what it is.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.330
There's money that you're going to need.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:17.500
So how much money do you currently have to
do this, and if you don't have the money,

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.500
how much money do you need to have in order
for you to be able to do this.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.500
Write that number down.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.720
Next, do you have the sticktoittiveness, because
this [the first 4 items] is fun to do.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.990
This is very fun to do.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.670
People love doing this exercise, up to this
point.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:35.160
The next one is not that much fun, because
most people don't stick to it.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.620
Most people are not willing to stick to it.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.130
Because this could be 11 years.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.130
[chuckle].

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.420
This could be 13 years.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.400
This could be seven years.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.090
This could be 24 months.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.090
People don't think that long.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.900
People are like, "I want it right now."

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.140
It doesn't work that way.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.390
This could be awhile until you're able to
go out there and do this.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:57.530
In sports teams, right now I was with Magic
Johnson, two weeks ago, and I was interviewing

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.530
him.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.530
I asked him a question.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.120
And I kind of cornered him with one of the
questions I asked him about Lakers and he

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.120
smiled.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.660
Two days later he announced that his meeting
with Jeannie Buss, he's now an adviser.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.610
Now Magic Johnson is trying to recruit Kobe
Bryant to be an adviser because he believes

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:14.750
they can put a team together where in the
next two to three years they can be a championship

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.750
contender.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.750
Two to three years.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.400
He didn't say in the next six months.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.260
Too often amateur entrepreneurs want it right
now.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.370
So watch this.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.370
What do they currently have?

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.770
Russell, certain athletes.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:25.770
What do they want to have?

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.770
Some superstars.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:28.100
Who do they need to outgun?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.290
Cleveland, Golden State.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.540
Do they have enough money?

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.540
Yes they do.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.400
Can they stick to it long term to be able
to get there.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.400
Yes.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.170
And last but not least, do you match the position
that you want to have?

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.170
What does that mean?

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.340
For instance.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.570
Matching the position.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:49.280
If I want to become the best financial adviser
in Silicon Valley, and I want to own the position

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.350
of people that are in the technology sector,
hypothetically.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:57.620
So, do I match that position to get them?

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.790
Do I look the part?

00:03:58.790 --> 00:03:59.960
Do I talk the part?

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.040
Do I walk the part?

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.930
Do I go to the places that they go to, the
country club that they belong to, the gym,

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.170
the equinox, the Neiman Marcus.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:11.840
Do I belong to that special nightclub that
they go to after hours.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.840
Do I belong to this?

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.130
Do I match that?

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.480
Am I matching that?

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.579
Or, if I don't care about that market, it's
a completely different market, and I'm trying

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:23.110
to connect with the middle America market,
do I dress up too preppy?

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.110
Am I too much?

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.120
Am I too flashy and I don't connect with middle
America?

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.830
Because middle America's like, dude, I wear
jeans and shirts.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.919
And you're over dressing for me too much,
and it's kind of intimidating.

00:04:32.919 --> 00:04:36.940
I've never put a suit on before and quite
frankly, I still don't know how to tie a tie.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.360
And you're trying to get me to - I don't know
about this guy.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.360
I don't relate to him.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:41.360
I don't connect with him.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.360
Do you match?

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.710
Hey, I want to get into the 25 year old market,
but I'm 63 years old.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.710
How am I going to do it?

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:47.710
I don't match.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:49.229
How am I going to position myself to do it?

00:04:49.229 --> 00:04:54.300
Once you answer these questions, and you go
through it, from there, if you can do this

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.041
[sticktoittiveness] and you put a timeline
to it, then more power to you.

00:04:57.041 --> 00:04:58.400
You go get it.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.650
If you can do this, if you do this, and you're
willing to stick around for the three years,

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.870
seven years, 10 years, 12 years, 15 years,
maybe some even 20 years, then eventually

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:12.330
you're going to be able to position yourself
to potentially one day dominate an industry,

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:16.039
whatever that industry may be, that you want
to position to dominate.

00:05:16.039 --> 00:05:18.350
So with that being said, Paul, throw us the
pillow.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.680
This is another short episode that we did.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:26.639
6 questions to ask for you to position yourself
to dominate an industry.

